.TH MARKOV 1 "November 2026" "Markov" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
markov \- declarative workflow engine for agents and native steps
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B markov
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Markov executes YAML workflows using native operations and optional external
tools. Workflows can run local shell commands and access configured services;
inspect a workflow before running it. Execute workflows as your normal user.
The package provides the engine, documentation, shell completions, and a local
quickstart. Agent CLIs, Kubernetes clients and credentials are not included.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "validate " "file.yaml|directory"
Validate a workflow file or a directory workflow.
.TP
.BI "run " "file.yaml|directory"
Run a workflow. External tools and service access depend on its steps.
.TP
.BI "resume " run_id
Resume a failed or paused workflow run.
.TP
.B list
List recorded workflow runs.
.TP
.BI "status " run_id
Show the status of a recorded run.
.TP
.B diagram
Generate a Mermaid diagram of a completed run.
.TP
.B schema
Print workflow fields and step parameters as JSON.
.TP
.B codify
Move agent work into validated native workflow steps. Consult the command's
help for its inputs, optional agent tools, and execution requirements.
.TP
.BI "completion " shell
Generate completion for bash, zsh, fish, or PowerShell.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help. Use \fBmarkov command --help\fR for command-specific options.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the engine version.
.TP
.BI "--state-store " "path-or-DSN"
For commands that operate on run state, select a SQLite path or PostgreSQL
DSN. The default SQLite file is \fB./markov-state.db\fR. Treat run-state files
and connection details as private data; package removal does not delete them.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run the packaged quickstart in a new writable directory:
.PP
.nf
mkdir markov-quickstart
cd markov-quickstart
cp /usr/share/markov/examples/quickstart.yaml .
markov validate quickstart.yaml
markov run quickstart.yaml
.fi
.PP
The workflow creates \fBquickstart-report.md\fR in the current directory.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /usr/share/markov/examples/quickstart.yaml
Credential-free local example workflow.
.TP
.B /usr/share/doc/markov/README.md
Project overview and documentation links.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1)
.PP
